{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וחי בהם", :translit "u'chai bahem", :gloss "and you shall live by them"} {:he "לא תקרבו לגלות ערוה", :translit "lo tikrevu legalot ervah", :gloss "you shall not approach to uncover nakedness"} {:he "יהרג ואל יעבור", :translit "yehareg ve'al ya'avor", :gloss "he is killed and does not transgress"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition (semikhut): the phrase 'and you shall live by them' is placed adjacent to the prohibition of uncovering nakedness, teaching that life does not override sexual prohibitions"}], :frame {:text "The principle 'yehareg ve'al ya'avor' — that one must be killed rather than transgress — is established for three sins in Sanhedrin 74a: idolatry, forbidden sexual relations, and murder. The Sages derive this specifically for forbidden sexual relations from Leviticus 18:5, the verse under discussion: 'you shall live by them' — and not die by them, teaching that where a sexual prohibition is at stake, one surrenders one's life rather than violate it.", :sources ["Sanhedrin 74a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition (semikhut): the phrase 'and you shall live by them' is placed adjacent to the prohibition of uncovering nakedness, teaching that life does not override sexual prohibitions", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:56.607737489Z", :model "glm-5.2"}